# NOTE: git does not strip trailing comments from pattern lines -- every comment
# here is on its own line deliberately.

# Environment
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# Large regenerable data. data/frames/ is 231 MB and is rebuilt by
# tools/extract_frames.py; it is labeling-only and the pipeline never reads it.
data/frames/
Videos-*.zip

# Superseded GT backup (pre id-fix). The audit log in docs/labeling-protocol.md
# records what changed, so the file itself need not ship.
data/ground_truth.pre-idfix.json

# Deliberately NOT ignored, and worth stating because each is easy to ignore
# by reflex:
#   outputs/          -- the required output artifact
#   experiments/      -- the run log (config.yaml + results.json per run)
#   data/vlm_cache/   -- committed so results reproduce without a GPU

# Source clips -- DELIBERATELY NOT SHIPPED (decided 2026-09-16).
# 89 MB of the task-setter's footage. The repo is public, and redistributing
# someone else's data is not ours to do. See README "Getting the data" for what
# a reviewer needs; the committed outputs, metrics and VLM cache make the
# results inspectable without the clips.
Videos/
